{"name":"Fright Night","hex":"#004499","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"fright","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A state of terror excited by the sudden appearance of danger; sudden and violent fear, usually of short duration; a sudden alarm.","Someone strange, ugly or shocking, producing a feeling of alarm or aversion."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To frighten."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fright"},{"term":"night","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The time when the Sun is below the horizon when the sky is dark.","The period of darkness beginning at the end of evening astronomical twilight when the sun is 18 degrees below the horizon, and ending at the beginning of morning astronomical twilight."]},{"part":"Interjection","definitions":["Ellipsis of good night."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/night"}],"entries":[{"title":"Fright Night","blocks":[{"text":"Fright Night is a 1985 American supernatural horror film written and directed by Tom Holland, in his directorial debut. The film follows teenager Charley Brewster, who discovers that his next-door neighbor Jerry Dandrige is a vampire. When no one else believes him, Charley decides to get Peter Vincent, a horror host who acted in films as a vampire hunter, to stop Jerry."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/e2/Fright_night_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fright_Night"},{"title":"Fright Night (2011 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Fright Night is a 2011 American supernatural horror film directed by Craig Gillespie and produced by Michael De Luca and Alison Rosenzweig. A remake of Tom Holland's 1985 film, the film's screenplay was adapted by Marti Noxon. It features Anton Yelchin, Colin Farrell, Toni Collette, Imogen Poots, Christopher Mintz-Plasse, and David Tennant. The plot follows a boy who discovers that his neighbor is actually a vampire, which culminates in a battle between the two."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/14/Fright_Night_%282011_film%29_poster.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fright_Night_(2011_film)"},{"title":"Night","blocks":[{"text":"Night, or nighttime, is the period of darkness when the Sun is below the horizon. Daylight illuminates one side of Earth, leaving the other in darkness. The opposite of nighttime is daytime. Earth's rotation causes the appearance of sunrise and sunset. Moonlight, airglow, starlight, and light pollution dimly illuminate night. The duration of day, night, and twilight varies depending on the time of year and the observer's latitude."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/Savault_Chapel_Under_Milky_Way_BLS.jpg/330px-Savault_Chapel_Under_Milky_Way_BLS.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Night"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/e2/Fright_night_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/e2/Fright_night_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFright_night_poster.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/1/14/Fright_Night_%282011_film%29_poster.png/250px-Fright_Night_%282011_film%29_poster.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/14/Fright_Night_%282011_film%29_poster.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/1/14/Fright_Night_%282011_film%29_poster.png/250px-Fright_Night_%282011_film%29_poster.png?u